      <h3>Selected Module: SQL Relational Databases</h3>
      <h3>Module-Specific Requirements</h3>
      <table border="1" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" style="border-collapse: collapse;"><tr><td style="background-color:#e2e3e5; font-weight:bold;">All of these are required</td><td style="background-color:#e2e3e5; font-weight:bold;">Completed?</td></tr><tr><td style="background-color:transparent; font-weight:normal;">You must create a database for your program to use including at least one table to store data into.</td><td style="background-color:#d4edda; font-weight:bold;">Yes</td></tr><tr><td style="background-color:transparent; font-weight:normal;">Your software must demonstrate the ability to insert, modify, delete, and retrieve (or query) data.</td><td style="background-color:#d4edda; font-weight:bold;">Yes</td></tr><tr><td style="background-color:transparent; font-weight:normal;">This module requires more than just creating the database and determining SQL commands. You must write software that builds the SQL commands, submits them, receives the results from the database, and uses the results in some way.</td><td style="background-color:#d4edda; font-weight:bold;">Yes</td></tr></table>
      <br>
      <table border="1" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" style="border-collapse: collapse;"><tr><td style="background-color:#e2e3e5; font-weight:bold;">One of these is required</td><td style="background-color:#e2e3e5; font-weight:bold;">Completed?</td></tr><tr><td style="background-color:transparent; font-weight:normal;">Add additional tables to your database and perform a join in your software between two of the tables.</td><td style="background-color:#d4edda; font-weight:bold;">Yes</td></tr><tr><td style="background-color:transparent; font-weight:normal;">Use at least two of the aggregate functions to summarize numerical data in your database.</td><td style="background-color:#d4edda; font-weight:bold;">Yes</td></tr><tr><td style="background-color:transparent; font-weight:normal;">Demonstrate the use of a column containing a date or time along with a query that demonstrates filtering within a date or time range.</td><td style="background-color:#d4edda; font-weight:bold;">Yes</td></tr></table>

